From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:58:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_cake: nat mode: no flow dissection for
 non-IPv4 with an L4 hash

In nat mode every packet was dissected so cake_update_flowkeys() could put
the conntrack tuple's addresses in its keys. That only rewrites IPv4: an
IPv6 packet (or any other) carrying an L4 hash keeps using the hash, and
since 760-01 the host hashes wait for a queue allocation, so its dissected
keys went unused. The Ethernet sets an L4 hash on what it receives, so
for IPv6 that was wasted work on every download packet.

Skip the dissection for them; the flow and host tags are unchanged.

KUnit: cake_test_hash_matches_eager now also runs the nat modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/sched/sch_cake.c      | 6 ++++++
 net/sched/sch_cake_test.c | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/sched/sch_cake.c b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
index d497066..ab4da23 100644
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -953,6 +953,12 @@ static u32 cake_hash(struct cake_tin_data *q, const struct sk_buff *skb,
 	if ((!hash_flows || (use_skbhash && !nat_enabled)) && !hosts_now)
 		goto skip_hash;
 
+	/* nat mode only rewrites IPv4 keys (cake_update_flowkeys()): anything
+	 * else with an L4 hash keeps it, and its keys would go unused
+	 */
+	if (use_skbhash && !hosts_now && skb_protocol(skb, true) != htons(ETH_P_IP))
+		goto skip_hash;
+
 	skb_flow_dissect_flow_keys(skb, &keys,
 				   FLOW_DISSECTOR_F_STOP_AT_FLOW_LABEL);
 
diff --git a/net/sched/sch_cake_test.c b/net/sched/sch_cake_test.c
index fcfaa88..36809ec 100644
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake_test.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake_test.c
@@ -170,6 +170,12 @@ static void cake_test_check_flow(struct kunit *test, struct cake_tin_data *q,
 static const int cake_test_modes[] = {
 	CAKE_FLOW_SRC_IP, CAKE_FLOW_DST_IP, CAKE_FLOW_HOSTS, CAKE_FLOW_FLOWS,
 	CAKE_FLOW_DUAL_SRC, CAKE_FLOW_DUAL_DST, CAKE_FLOW_TRIPLE,
+	/* nat: no conntrack here, so the keys stay the packet's; IPv6 (and
+	 * IPv4 without a conntrack entry) with an L4 hash keeps the hash
+	 */
+	CAKE_FLOW_FLOWS | CAKE_FLOW_NAT_FLAG,
+	CAKE_FLOW_DUAL_DST | CAKE_FLOW_NAT_FLAG,
+	CAKE_FLOW_TRIPLE | CAKE_FLOW_NAT_FLAG,
 };
 
 /* First packet (queue allocated), next packets (direct hit), for 3 hosts x
